bsh-shell (5.14.0-1) noble; urgency=medium

  * BrightLink v1.1: ship the geo + push surface end-to-end.
    - New `link-geo` shell builtin in the bsh/brightlink module with
      five subcommands (status, proximity, zone, get, refresh)
      mapping 1:1 to RFC §9 LINK_GEO_* commands. Supports `--json`
      for machine-readable output and `--format wgs84|brightspace|both`
      for LINK_GEO_GET.
    - WGS84 ↔ ECEF ↔ BrightSpace coordinate pipeline (RFC §6.3) with
      exact-by-definition constants. Verified against the BrightSpace
      doc's published GODE (NASA GSFC, ITRF2020 epoch 2015.0) anchor.
    - Drops the legacy Scripts/bsh-geo and Scripts/bsh-geo-override
      stub scripts (functionally replaced by the new builtin).
  * Drop all SDI / OSC 7777 references throughout the tree.
    BrightLink is the protocol; clean slate. Removes Test/V16sdi.ztst
    and the three Test/sdi_*.py helpers; no functional change to the
    shell itself.

 -- Jessica Mulein <jessica@digitaldefiance.org>  Fri, 22 May 2026 12:00:00 +0000

bsh-shell (5.13.0-1) noble; urgency=medium

  * ls builtin: support GNU-style long options, in particular
    --color[=WHEN] with WHEN in {auto,always,never,tty,if-tty,
    yes,no,none,force}.  --color overrides -G and the default
    isatty() detection.
  * Document the ls builtin in Doc/Bsh/mod_files.yo, covering all
    supported short options (-acdFGhLlnorstu) plus --color.

 -- Jessica Mulein <jessica@digitaldefiance.org>  Thu, 21 May 2026 12:00:00 +0000

bsh-shell (5.12.2-1) noble; urgency=medium

  * Add ls -c (ctime sort and display) to the bsh files module builtin.
  * Fix bsh-newuser-install option (2): guard cp with -r readability check.
  * Add Oh My Bsh, bsh-iputils, and bsh-findutils recommendations to
    bsh-newuser-install completion flow.

